  "answers": {
    "netmedex_hybrid_rag": "**Direct evidence for each hop**\n\n* **Dysbiosis → Periodontitis** – Metatranscriptomic data show that shifts in oral microbial composition (dysbiosis) precede clinical progression of periodontitis【PMID:25918553】. A review of oral pathobionts also describes dysbiosis as a driver of alveolar bone loss in periodontitis【PMID:24646638】. (human, in‑vivo)\n\n* **Periodontitis is a Inflammation** – Periodontitis is defined as a polymicrobial biofilm‑induced inflammatory disease affecting millions of people【PMID:25918553】. Animal‑model work confirms that bacterial‑triggered inflammation is central to periodontal bone loss【PMID:25574929】. (human & animal)\n\n* **Inflammation → Osteoporosis** – Chronic inflammatory states have been shown to promote systemic bone loss and osteoporosis through cytokine‑mediated activation of osteoclasts【PMID:22179898】. (human, clinical)\n\n* **Osteoporosis → Bone loss** – Post‑menopausal osteoporosis expands the osteoclastic pool, causing generalized skeletal bone loss, including the jaw【PMID:20599675】. (human, clinical)\n\n**Overall mechanistic inference**\n\nThe four‑step chain (dysbiosis → periodontitis → inflammation → osteoporosis → bone loss) is not demonstrated in a single study; it is assembled from the above direct pieces of evidence. Thus the complete pathway remains a **multi‑hop inference** rather than a single‑experiment observation.\n\n---\n\n### Graph‑derived candidate insights\n* dysbiosis leads_to periodontitis – PATH 5392416d32ad795a, PMID 25918553 (**direct evidence**) – GRAPH‑INCREMENTAL CANDIDATE  \n* periodontitis is_a inflammation – PATH 5392416d32ad795a, PMID 25918553 (**direct evidence**) – GRAPH‑INCREMENTAL CANDIDATE  \n* inflammation induces osteoporosis – PATH 5392416d32ad795a, PMID 22179898 (**direct evidence**) –"
  },
